              "rationale": "The <html> element in about.html has no lang attribute, so screen readers have to guess which language to use for pronunciation. All of the page's text is in English: the title, headings, paragraph, form label and button. So lang=\"en\" fits. I searched the rest of the site for a lang value to match, such as en-GB or en-US, but found none, so I used plain \"en\". A reviewer can change it to a regional code if the site prefers one. This fixes this one finding. It does not make the whole page accessible.",
